"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f217c016c7c203a14cec0d5879cb22a0b80bebbf1d0eeb7bce1e0451333f2390", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this Chapter, we discuss <ACCENT_0001>tale morphisms of schemes. We illustrate\nsome of the more important concepts by working with the Noetherian case.\nOur principal goal is to collect for the reader enough commutative\nalgebra results to start reading a treatise on <ACCENT_0002>tale cohomology. An\nauxiliary goal is to provide enough evidence to ensure that the reader stops\ncalling the phrase ``the <ACCENT_0003>tale topology of schemes'' an exercise in general\nnonsense, if (s)he does indulge in such blasphemy.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cdfeac125c516da7a1bdf3baa737da4739862d1eada81099ebb38533279ee627", "unit_id": "inventory:etale:024K:paragraph/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale:inventory:etale:024K:section_title/0001", "hash": "sha256:d9b07d70072796b234cb6d965b3f078249e4428e3d50475fb90cade145d14872", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 218, "byte_start": 167, "file": "etale.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:818b11324e818fe49df54475c6acdad873cdb21ec9d6e3fdc16fee24d3904974", "line_end": 19, "line_start": 18}, "owner_tag": "024K", "parent_tag": "024K", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "024K", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{section-introduction}", "TEXTCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTOPEN_0001": "\\section{"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e